From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:22:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: Save, Save As and AutoSave write the file away from
 the interface

With a host that provides Services::run_detached, a save takes the workbook's snapshot in the frame it is asked in, hands serializing and writing to the host, and records the result in the frame after it is done (the engine's save_job). The window keeps drawing and taking input meanwhile, and an edit made while the file is written stays unsaved.

One file is written by one job at a time, also for two workbooks saving to one path. An explicit save asked for while its workbook or file is being written waits and then writes the workbook as it is by then; an AutoSave in that case is left out. A failed save is shown and leaves the workbook open and unsaved. "Save" in Save Changes? closes the workbook after the file is written and asks again when it was edited meanwhile. The window does not close while a save is on its way. A host that cannot take a job gets it run at once.

Unchanged: without the service, while actions are recorded, a macro is debugged or an undo group is open, for a PDF, for a workbook without a file and for control channel requests, file.save is one call.

Tests: tests/save_jobs.rs (13). Not covered by a test: the window close held back while a save is on its way.
